; Sprite shift pairs and the frame tables of the monk
;
; The 16-pixel-wide sprites of the monk (and of most enemies) are stored in the sprite sheet (#R$D700) as four copies
; of each frame, each shifted two pixels further right than the one before, so that a sprite can be placed on any
; 2-pixel column without shifting at run time. X mod 4 (X in 2-pixel units) selects the copy; the pair table gives, per
; copy, the column offset inside the frame and the width in bytes (2 for the unshifted copy, 3 for the others: 2 + 3 + 3 +
; 3 = 11 columns per frame). The monk frame tables hold the sprite sheet address of each frame (D = pixel row page, E
; = first column); #R$AC1C picks the table by the facing (#R$A897) and the entry by the animation frame (#R$A896).
; .
; +$00 ShiftPairs: 4 x (byte offset of the copy, width) for X mod 0, 1, 2, 3, shared with the enemies
; +$08 MonkFramesLeft: 3 words, facing left (#R$A897 = 1): walking 0, walking 1, in the air
; +$0E MonkFramesRight: 3 words, facing right: walking 0, walking 1, in the air
; +$14 MonkDyingFrames: 7 words, the dying animation (3 pictures, repeated, #R$AA3D)
; +$22 ShiftPairsCrouch: 4 x (offset, width) for the crouching monk (3 bytes wide in every phase)
; +$2A CrouchFramesLeft: 2 words, crouching facing left (sprite sheet rows 24-39)
; +$2E CrouchFramesRight: 2 words, crouching facing right
@label=ShiftPairs
b$AC9F DEFB $00,$02                                   ; {Standing: (byte
 $ACA1 DEFB $02,$03                                   ; offset, width) for X
 $ACA3 DEFB $05,$03                                   ; mod 4
 $ACA5 DEFB $08,$03                                   ; }
@label=MonkFramesLeft
 $ACA7 DEFW $D700,$D70B,$D716                         ; Standing frames, facing
                                                      ; left
@label=MonkFramesRight
 $ACAD DEFW $D721,$D72C,$D737                         ; Standing frames, facing
                                                      ; right
@label=MonkDyingFrames
 $ACB3 DEFW $D742,$D74D,$D742,$D74D,$D758,$D74D,$D758 ; Dying frames
@label=ShiftPairsCrouch
 $ACC1 DEFB $00,$03                                   ; {Crouching: (byte
 $ACC3 DEFB $03,$03                                   ; offset, width) for X
 $ACC5 DEFB $06,$03                                   ; mod 4
 $ACC7 DEFB $09,$03                                   ; }
@label=CrouchFramesLeft
 $ACC9 DEFW $EF00,$EF0C                               ; Crouching frames,
                                                      ; facing left
@label=CrouchFramesRight
 $ACCD DEFW $EF18,$EF24                               ; Crouching frames,
                                                      ; facing right
